@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@
+# Logging taxonomy
+
+PegaFila splits observability into **archive** logs, **audit** trails, and
+**Discord alerts**. Discord is never a Monolog channel — see
+[`DiscordOpsAlert`](../../app/Ops/DiscordOpsAlert.php) and
+[business-rules Observability](../business-rules.md).
+
+**Rule of thumb for agents:** if you would not wake someone at 2am, it is not Discord.
+
+## Destinations
+
+| Lane | What it is | Sink | Discord? |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| **Archive** | Normal app logs (debug→error), request noise, caught exceptions, soft-fails | Daily rotating `storage/logs/laravel-*.log` (`daily` channel, default stack) | **No** |
+| **Audit** | Durable “what changed / who tried” trail | Daily rotating `storage/logs/audit-*.log` (`Log::channel('audit')`) | **No** |
+| **Alert** | Human-pageable ops incident | `App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert::send()` | **Yes** (and also `Log::…` to archive) |
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+  event[App_event]
+  decide{AI_decision_matrix}
+  archive[archive_daily_log]
+  audit[audit_channel_file]
+  discord[DiscordOpsAlert]
+  event --> decide
+  decide -->|routine_debug_info_warn_error_trace| archive
+  decide -->|security_billing_auth_trail| audit
+  decide -->|ops_incident_needs_human_now| discord
+  discord -.->|always_also| archive
+  audit -.->|never| discord
+```
+
+## AI decision matrix
+
+**Use Discord (`DiscordOpsAlert`) when all are true:**
+
+1. Operational / infrastructure / money-path failure (not UX validation).
+2. Actionable by a human (restart worker, check Asaas, raise plan limit).
+3. Not high-frequency per request (no per-ticket, per-HTTP 422).
+4. Context is redaction-safe (no secrets; `DiscordOpsAlert` redacts sensitive keys).
+
+| Destination | Examples |
+| --- | --- |
+| **Discord** | Job failed after retries exhausted; Asaas webhook invalid token / permanent processing failure; payment charge create failed at gateway; queue worker crash loop; plan limit blocking entity ops; deploy/smoke health fail |
+| **Archive only** | `Log::debug`/`info` traces; validation errors; 404s; Telescope noise; Discord soft-fail (`Discord ops alert failed`); expected business rejects (inactive queue) |
+| **Audit** (not Discord) | Login failure / lockout (when auth lands); membership role changes; subscription status transitions; webhook received + idempotent skip/apply outcome |
+
+## How to write
+
+```php
+// Archive (default stack → daily)
+Log::warning('Ticket issue skipped', ['reason' => 'inactive_queue']);
+
+// Audit (specialized file — never Discord)
+Log::channel('audit')->info('Subscription status changed', [
+    'subscription_id' => $id,
+    'from' => $from,
+    'to' => $to,
+]);
+
+// Alert: always pair archive Log with DiscordOpsAlert
+Log::error('Asaas webhook processing failed', ['payment_id' => $id]);
+app(\App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert::class)->send(
+    'Asaas webhook failed',
+    'Processing failed after receive',
+    ['payment_id' => $id],
+);
+```
+
+Do **not** add a `discord` entry under `config/logging.php` channels. Do **not** wire every exception to Discord.
+
+## Config / retention
+
+| Env | Purpose | Default |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `LOG_CHANNEL` | Default channel | `stack` |
+| `LOG_STACK` | Stack members (archive) | `daily` |
+| `LOG_LEVEL` | Archive level | `debug` |
+| `LOG_DAILY_DAYS` | Archive retention days | `14` |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL` | Audit minimum level | `info` |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_DAYS` | Audit retention days | `90` |
+| `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` | Alert webhook (empty = no-op) | _(empty)_ |
+
+Files live under `storage/logs/` (`laravel-YYYY-MM-DD.log`, `audit-YYYY-MM-DD.log`). Do not commit them.
+
+The VPS currently overrides the default channel with `LOG_CHANNEL=stderr` in
+`docker/compose.vps.yml`, so routine application logs go to container output
+instead of `laravel-*.log`. The explicit `audit` channel remains available and
+writes `audit-*.log`.
+
+## Related
+
+- Discord client usage: [`docs/ops/devops.md`](devops.md) (Discord ops alerts)
+- Secrets: never log API keys, webhook URLs, or passwords (AGENTS.md / Asaas skill)
